What is Robot Operating System (ROS)?
Robot Operating System (ROS) is a flexible, open-source framework that serves as an essential foundation for developing advanced robotics software. It provides a comprehensive suite of tools including hardware abstraction, message-passing infrastructure, device drivers, libraries, visualizers, and package management systems, enabling seamless integration across diverse robotic hardware and applications. Key components encompass communication middleware, navigation stacks, perception modules, manipulation libraries, and simulation environments, collectively empowering developers to build sophisticated autonomous systems with unprecedented efficiency and scalability.
